IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-groups`
IMPORT `sgd-compromise`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: Part 7, ss 215, 215AA and 215AB.
-- The power to acquire the shares of shareholders dissenting from a scheme or contract approved by a 90% majority (s 215); joint offers (s 215AA);
-- the effect of the impossibility of communicating or accepting an offer (s 215AB).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes a person's point of view; the seat layer (sgd-seat.l4) does.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29 and the Guide's rulings; see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sgd)").
--   JUST TRUE   the section's own test is met on the facts given.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no to this case in its own words (a "means" definition, a condition introduced by "if", "unless",
--               "until"; a list closed with "only"; a flat negative; a period or "where" condition the text states).
--   NOTHING     not covered: the text lists without closing the list, says "includes", is silent, points to a power or
--               instrument outside the sources, or limits a grant in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every branch that answers no carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`; every branch that answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- Periods are counted only by sg-periods.l4 (conventions P1 to P9 of the keel: assumed, not ruled by a lawyer).
-- The Official Receiver is the party `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver`, declared once in sgd-compromise.l4 at its first use.
-- The Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 is not a source: what section 197 of it does is not read here.
-- A share is counted as a NUMBER of shares. A date is written Date day month year.

§ `Section 215(1): the offer approved by the holders of 90% of the shares`

-- Heading (lines 20592-20593): "Power to acquire shares of shareholders dissenting from scheme or contract approved by 90% majority": not operative.

-- What the scheme or contract involves: s 215(1) speaks of "all of the shares" or "all of the shares in any particular class", and of nothing less.
DECLARE `s 215(1) what the scheme or contract involves` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(1) the transfer of all of the shares in the company`
    `s 215(1) the transfer of all of the shares in a particular class in the company`
    `s 215(1) a transfer of some only of the shares`

-- The counts the 90% is made of, as a witness could state them from the register of members and the offer.
-- "Disregarded" shares (subsection (1C)) are not subtracted from the approving holders' count by this record: the caller states the number of the counted
-- shares whose holders approved (fork F-215-1: the text says the shares are "disregarded" without saying on which side of the fraction).
DECLARE `s 215(1) share count` HAS
    `s 215(1) the number of the shares in the company, or in the class, in issue, treasury shares included` IS A NUMBER
    `s 215(1) the number of those shares held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
    `s 215(1C)(a) the number of those shares issued after the date of the offer, other than pursuant to the exercise of an option or right attached to a convertible security issued on or before the date of the offer by the transferor company` IS A NUMBER
    `s 215(1C)(b) the number of relevant treasury shares that have ceased to be held as treasury shares after the date of the offer` IS A NUMBER
    `s 215(1) the number of those shares already held at the date of the offer by the transferee` IS A NUMBER
    `s 215(1) the number of the shares counted whose holders have approved the offer` IS A NUMBER

-- The two limbs and the case outside them: "all of the shares or all of the shares in any particular class".
GIVEN involves IS A `s 215(1) what the scheme or contract involves`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215(1) the scheme or contract involves the transfer of all of the shares or of all of the shares in a particular class` MEANS
    CONSIDER involves
    WHEN `s 215(1) the transfer of all of the shares in the company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 215(1) the transfer of all of the shares in a particular class in the company` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "(other than shares already held at the date of the offer by the transferee ...)" stands in the class limb only (fork F-215-2, marginal reading for a lawyer):
-- read literally, the shares the transferee already holds are left out of the count only where the scheme is for all the shares of a class.
GIVEN involves IS A `s 215(1) what the scheme or contract involves`
      counts IS A `s 215(1) share count`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215(1) the number of shares already held by the transferee that are left out of the count` MEANS
    CONSIDER involves
    WHEN `s 215(1) the transfer of all of the shares in a particular class in the company` THEN counts's `s 215(1) the number of those shares already held at the date of the offer by the transferee`
    OTHERWISE 0

-- The total the 90% is a fraction of: the shares in issue, less treasury shares, less the shares subsection (1C) says to disregard, less (class limb) the transferee's own.
GIVEN involves IS A `s 215(1) what the scheme or contract involves`
      counts IS A `s 215(1) share count`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215(1) the total number of the shares the 90% is counted against` MEANS
    (((((counts's `s 215(1) the number of the shares in the company, or in the class, in issue, treasury shares included`)
        MINUS (counts's `s 215(1) the number of those shares held as treasury shares`))
        MINUS (counts's `s 215(1C)(a) the number of those shares issued after the date of the offer, other than pursuant to the exercise of an option or right attached to a convertible security issued on or before the date of the offer by the transferor company`))
        MINUS (counts's `s 215(1C)(b) the number of relevant treasury shares that have ceased to be held as treasury shares after the date of the offer`))
        MINUS (`s 215(1) the number of shares already held by the transferee that are left out of the count` involves counts))

-- (1): "Where a scheme or contract involving the transfer of all of the shares or all of the shares in any particular class ... has, within 4 months after the making of the offer ...,
-- been approved ... by the holders of not less than 90% of the total number of those shares ...". "within 4 months after": the window opens the day after the offer (P2; fork F-215-3).
-- src:20595 | 215.—(1) Where a scheme or contract involving the transfer of all
-- src:20596 | of the shares or all of the shares in any particular class in a company
-- src:20597 | (called in this section the transferor company) to a person (called in
-- src:20598 | this section the transferee) has, within 4 months after the making of
-- src:20599 | the offer in that behalf by the transferee, been approved as to the
-- src:20600 | shares or as to each class of shares whose transfer is involved by the
-- src:20601 | holders of not less than 90% of the total number of those shares
-- src:20602 | (excluding treasury shares) or of the shares of that class (other than
-- src:20603 | shares already held at the date of the offer by the transferee, and
-- src:20604 | excluding any shares in the transferor company held as treasury
-- src:20605 | shares), the transferee may at any time within 2 months, after the offer
@ref s 215(1) approval (src:20595-20605)
GIVEN involves IS A `s 215(1) what the scheme or contract involves`
      counts IS A `s 215(1) share count`
      `the day the offer was made by the transferee` IS A DATE
      `the day the holders of the requisite number of the shares had approved the offer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1) the scheme or contract has been approved by the holders of the requisite number of the shares` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 215(1) the scheme or contract involves the transfer of all of the shares or of all of the shares in a particular class` involves)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a scheme or contract involving the transfer of all of the shares or all of the shares in any particular class in a company" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))
    ELSE IF NOT (`period: the date is within a period after` `the day the offer was made by the transferee` `the day the holders of the requisite number of the shares had approved the offer` 4 Months)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has, within 4 months after the making of the offer in that behalf by the transferee, been approved" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling (a); fork F-215-3)
         ELSE IF    ((`s 215(1) the total number of the shares the 90% is counted against` involves counts) GREATER THAN 0)
                AND (((counts's `s 215(1) the number of the shares counted whose holders have approved the offer`) TIMES 100) AT LEAST ((`s 215(1) the total number of the shares the 90% is counted against` involves counts) TIMES 90))
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "been approved as to the shares or as to each class of shares whose transfer is involved by the holders of not less than 90% of the total number of those shares" (the approval the subsection asks for, not reached)

-- (1): the transferee "may at any time within 2 months, after the offer has been so approved, give notice in the prescribed manner to any dissenting shareholder that it desires to acquire the dissenting shareholder’s shares".
-- A power ("may") gated by a "where" and by a period: JUST FALSE by the periods ruling (a) and (b), listed in the fork register (F-215-4); a shareholder who is not dissenting is outside the grant (NOTHING, scope limit, periods ruling (c)).
-- src:20595 | 215.—(1) Where a scheme or contract involving the transfer of all
-- src:20596 | of the shares or all of the shares in any particular class in a company
-- src:20597 | (called in this section the transferor company) to a person (called in
-- src:20598 | this section the transferee) has, within 4 months after the making of
-- src:20599 | the offer in that behalf by the transferee, been approved as to the
-- src:20600 | shares or as to each class of shares whose transfer is involved by the
-- src:20601 | holders of not less than 90% of the total number of those shares
-- src:20602 | (excluding treasury shares) or of the shares of that class (other than
-- src:20603 | shares already held at the date of the offer by the transferee, and
-- src:20604 | excluding any shares in the transferor company held as treasury
-- src:20605 | shares), the transferee may at any time within 2 months, after the offer
-- src:20606 | has been so approved, give notice in the prescribed manner to any
-- src:20607 | dissenting shareholder that it desires to acquire the dissenting
-- src:20608 | shareholder’s shares; and when such a notice is given the
@ref s 215(1) notice (src:20595-20608)
GIVEN `the scheme or contract has been approved as subsection (1) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the offer was so approved` IS A DATE
      `the day the transferee gave the notice` IS A DATE
      `the shareholder is a dissenting shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1) the transferee may give notice to the dissenting shareholder that it desires to acquire the shares` MEANS
    IF NOT `the scheme or contract has been approved as subsection (1) requires`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a scheme or contract ... has ... been approved ... the transferee may" (split site (ii): a "where" gate on a power; periods ruling (b); fork F-215-4)
    ELSE IF NOT (`period: the date is within a period after` `the day the offer was so approved` `the day the transferee gave the notice` 2 Months)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may at any time within 2 months, after the offer has been so approved, give notice" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling (a); fork F-215-4)
         ELSE IF NOT `the shareholder is a dissenting shareholder`
              THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "give notice in the prescribed manner to any dissenting shareholder" (a grant naming dissenting shareholders; a notice to anyone else is outside it, periods ruling (c))
              ELSE IF `the notice is given in the prescribed manner`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources): "give notice in the prescribed manner" (the manner is prescribed under another instrument, not among the sources; s 4(1) "prescribed")

-- (1): "(1) ... the later of one month from the date on which the notice was given or 14 days of a statement being supplied": the last day of the period for the shareholder's application to the Court
-- (subsection (1)) and for the election between terms (subsection (1A)). "Supplied" is read as the day the statement was posted (subsection (2)): fork F-215-5.
-- src:20609 | transferee is, unless on an application made by the dissenting
-- src:20610 | shareholder within one month from the date on which the notice was
-- src:20611 | given or within 14 days of a statement being supplied to a dissenting
-- src:20612 | shareholder pursuant to subsection (2) (whichever is the later) the
@ref s 215(1) period (src:20609-20612)
GIVEN `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 215(1) the last day of one month from the date on which the notice was given` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` 1 Months

GIVEN `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 215(1) the last day of 14 days of a statement being supplied` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2)` 14 Days

GIVEN `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 215(1) the last day of the later of the one month and the 14 days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 215(1) the last day of one month from the date on which the notice was given` `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)`
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF (`s 215(1) the last day of 14 days of a statement being supplied` d) GREATER THAN (`s 215(1) the last day of one month from the date on which the notice was given` `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)`)
        THEN `s 215(1) the last day of 14 days of a statement being supplied` d
        ELSE `s 215(1) the last day of one month from the date on which the notice was given` `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)`

-- (1): "unless on an application made by the dissenting shareholder within one month from the date on which the notice was given or within 14 days of a statement being supplied ... (whichever is the later)":
-- the application is in time up to and including the last day.
-- src:20609 | transferee is, unless on an application made by the dissenting
-- src:20610 | shareholder within one month from the date on which the notice was
-- src:20611 | given or within 14 days of a statement being supplied to a dissenting
-- src:20612 | shareholder pursuant to subsection (2) (whichever is the later) the
@ref s 215(1) application (src:20609-20612)
GIVEN `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the dissenting shareholder applied to the Court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1) the dissenting shareholder's application to the Court is within the time subsection (1) allows` MEANS
    IF `the day the dissenting shareholder applied to the Court` AT MOST (`s 215(1) the last day of the later of the one month and the 14 days` `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on an application made by the dissenting shareholder within one month from the date on which the notice was given or within 14 days of a statement being supplied ... (whichever is the later)" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling (a))

-- (1): "unless on an application ... the Court thinks fit to order otherwise": the Court's power on a timely application. "On an application" is read as "upon", which counts as "where" (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05): JUST FALSE where there is none or it is late;
-- where the Court does not think fit, the grant is limited by its own wording: NOTHING (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-215-6).
-- src:20609 | transferee is, unless on an application made by the dissenting
-- src:20610 | shareholder within one month from the date on which the notice was
-- src:20611 | given or within 14 days of a statement being supplied to a dissenting
-- src:20612 | shareholder pursuant to subsection (2) (whichever is the later) the
-- src:20613 | Court thinks fit to order otherwise, entitled and bound to acquire
@ref s 215(1) the Court (src:20609-20613)
GIVEN `the dissenting shareholder has applied to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is within the time subsection (1) allows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks fit to order otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1) the Court may order that the transferee is not entitled and bound to acquire the shares` MEANS
    IF NOT `the dissenting shareholder has applied to the Court`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless on an application made by the dissenting shareholder" (split site (ii): "on an application" is read as "upon", which counts as "where": ruling (c) of 2026-11-05; fork F-215-6)
    ELSE IF NOT `the application is within the time subsection (1) allows`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within one month from the date on which the notice was given or within 14 days of a statement being supplied" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling (a))
         ELSE IF `the Court thinks fit to order otherwise`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court thinks fit to order otherwise" (a grant limited by the Court's own judgment; grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-215-6)

-- (1): "when such a notice is given the transferee is, unless ... the Court thinks fit to order otherwise, entitled and bound to acquire those shares". An "entitled" function: listed, not changed (grant ruling, limit 3; fork F-215-7).
-- The "unless" once met (the Court has ordered otherwise on a timely application): JUST FALSE, an "unless" condition read as the text's own no (case-by-case, fork F-215-7).
-- src:20608 | shareholder’s shares; and when such a notice is given the
-- src:20609 | transferee is, unless on an application made by the dissenting
-- src:20610 | shareholder within one month from the date on which the notice was
-- src:20611 | given or within 14 days of a statement being supplied to a dissenting
-- src:20612 | shareholder pursuant to subsection (2) (whichever is the later) the
-- src:20613 | Court thinks fit to order otherwise, entitled and bound to acquire
-- src:20614 | those shares on the terms which, under the scheme or contract the
@ref s 215(1) entitled (src:20608-20614)
GIVEN `the transferee has given the notice under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dissenting shareholder applied to the Court within the time subsection (1) allows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks fit to order otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1) the transferee is entitled and bound to acquire the dissenting shareholder's shares` MEANS
    IF NOT `the transferee has given the notice under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when such a notice is given the transferee is ... entitled and bound to acquire those shares" ("when" counts as "where": ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)
    ELSE IF `the dissenting shareholder applied to the Court within the time subsection (1) allows` AND `the Court thinks fit to order otherwise`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless on an application made by the dissenting shareholder ... the Court thinks fit to order otherwise" (an "unless" once met; fork F-215-7)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (1): "on the terms which, under the scheme or contract the shares of the approving shareholders are to be transferred to the transferee or if the offer contained 2 or more alternative sets of terms upon the terms which were specified in
-- the offer as being applicable to dissenting shareholders". With (1A) (the shareholder's election) and (1B) (the transferee's statement of the terms that apply on a failure to elect).
-- The terms "specified in the offer as being applicable to dissenting shareholders" are read as the terms (1B) makes the offer state (fork F-215-8).
DECLARE `s 215(1) terms` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(1) the terms on which the shares of the approving shareholders are to be transferred to the transferee`
    `s 215(1A) the terms the dissenting shareholder has elected`
    `s 215(1B) the terms the offer stated are to apply where the dissenting shareholder fails to elect in time`

-- src:20614 | those shares on the terms which, under the scheme or contract the
-- src:20615 | shares of the approving shareholders are to be transferred to the
-- src:20616 | transferee or if the offer contained 2 or more alternative sets of terms
-- src:20617 | upon the terms which were specified in the offer as being applicable
-- src:20618 | to dissenting shareholders.
@ref s 215(1) terms (src:20614-20618)
GIVEN `the offer contained 2 or more alternative sets of terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dissenting shareholder elected in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 215(1) terms`
`s 215(1) the terms on which the transferee must acquire the dissenting shareholder's shares` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offer contained 2 or more alternative sets of terms`
    THEN `s 215(1) the terms on which the shares of the approving shareholders are to be transferred to the transferee`
    ELSE IF `the dissenting shareholder elected in time`
         THEN `s 215(1A) the terms the dissenting shareholder has elected`
         ELSE `s 215(1B) the terms the offer stated are to apply where the dissenting shareholder fails to elect in time`

§ `Section 215(1A) and (1B): alternative terms`

-- (1A): "Where alternative terms were offered to the shareholders, a dissenting shareholder is entitled to elect not later than the end of one month after the date on which the notice is given under subsection (1),
-- or 14 days after a statement is supplied under subsection (2), whichever is the later, which of those terms the dissenting shareholder prefers." An "entitled" function (fork F-215-7).
-- src:20622 | (1A) Where alternative terms were offered to the shareholders, a
-- src:20623 | dissenting shareholder is entitled to elect not later than the end of
-- src:20624 | one month after the date on which the notice is given under
-- src:20629 | subsection (1), or 14 days after a statement is supplied under
-- src:20630 | subsection (2), whichever is the later, which of those terms the
-- src:20631 | dissenting shareholder prefers.
@ref s 215(1A) (src:20622-20631)
GIVEN `alternative terms were offered to the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the dissenting shareholder elected` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1A) the dissenting shareholder is entitled to elect which of the terms the shareholder prefers` MEANS
    IF NOT `alternative terms were offered to the shareholders`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where alternative terms were offered to the shareholders, a dissenting shareholder is entitled to elect" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))
    ELSE IF `the day the dissenting shareholder elected` AT MOST (`s 215(1) the last day of the later of the one month and the 14 days` `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "entitled to elect not later than the end of one month after the date on which the notice is given under subsection (1), or 14 days after a statement is supplied under subsection (2), whichever is the later" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling (a))

-- (1B): "In offering alternative terms to the shareholders, the transferee must state which of those terms is to apply to the acquisition of the shares of a dissenting shareholder where the dissenting shareholder fails
-- to make the election within the time allowed under subsection (1A)." A duty with no time limit: no breach path (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (sgd)").
-- src:20635 | (1B) In offering alternative terms to the shareholders, the transferee
-- src:20636 | must state which of those terms is to apply to the acquisition of the
-- src:20637 | shares of a dissenting shareholder where the dissenting shareholder
-- src:20638 | fails to make the election within the time allowed under
-- src:20639 | subsection (1A).
@ref s 215(1B) (src:20635-20639)
GIVEN `the offer contains alternative terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer states which of those terms is to apply where the dissenting shareholder fails to elect in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1B) the transferee has stated which of the terms is to apply on a failure to elect` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offer contains alternative terms`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In offering alternative terms to the shareholders, the transferee must state" (a "where" condition on a duty; periods ruling (b), marginal reading (a))
    ELSE IF `the offer states which of those terms is to apply where the dissenting shareholder fails to elect in time`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the transferee must state which of those terms is to apply" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)

§ `Section 215(1C) to (1E): which shares are counted`

-- (1C)(a): "shares that are issued after the date of the offer are to be disregarded unless they have been issued pursuant to the exercise of an option or right attached to any convertible security
-- that was issued on or before the date of the offer by the transferor company". "Unless" once met: the shares are counted, JUST FALSE as to disregard.
-- src:20643 | (1C) In determining whether the scheme or contract has been
-- src:20644 | approved by the holders of the requisite number of the shares, or
-- src:20645 | shares of any particular class, under subsection (1) —
-- src:20647 | (a) shares that are issued after the date of the offer are to be
-- src:20648 | disregarded unless they have been issued pursuant to the
-- src:20649 | exercise of an option or right attached to any convertible
-- src:20650 | security that was issued on or before the date of the offer by
-- src:20651 | the transferor company; and
@ref s 215(1C)(a) (src:20643-20651)
GIVEN `the shares were issued after the date of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares were issued pursuant to the exercise of an option or right attached to a convertible security that was issued on or before the date of the offer by the transferor company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1C)(a) the shares are to be disregarded` MEANS
    IF NOT `the shares were issued after the date of the offer`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shares that are issued after the date of the offer are to be disregarded" (the subsection says nothing of shares issued on or before the date of the offer; periods ruling (c))
    ELSE IF `the shares were issued pursuant to the exercise of an option or right attached to a convertible security that was issued on or before the date of the offer by the transferor company`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are to be disregarded unless they have been issued pursuant to the exercise of an option or right attached to any convertible security that was issued on or before the date of the offer" (an "unless" once met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (1D): "In subsection (1C)(b), “relevant treasury shares” means (a) shares that are held by the transferor company as treasury shares on the date of the offer; or (b) shares that become shares held ... as
-- treasury shares after the date of the offer but before a date specified in or determined in accordance with the terms of the offer." A "means" definition.
-- src:20658 | (1D) In subsection (1C)(b), “relevant treasury shares” means —
-- src:20660 | (a) shares that are held by the transferor company as treasury
-- src:20661 | shares on the date of the offer; or
-- src:20663 | (b) shares that become shares held by the transferor company
-- src:20664 | as treasury shares after the date of the offer but before a
-- src:20665 | date specified in or determined in accordance with the
-- src:20666 | terms of the offer.
@ref s 215(1D) (src:20658-20666)
GIVEN `the shares are held by the transferor company as treasury shares on the date of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares become shares held by the transferor company as treasury shares after the date of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares become so held before a date specified in or determined in accordance with the terms of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1D) the shares are relevant treasury shares` MEANS
    IF    `the shares are held by the transferor company as treasury shares on the date of the offer`
       OR (`the shares become shares held by the transferor company as treasury shares after the date of the offer` AND `the shares become so held before a date specified in or determined in accordance with the terms of the offer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant treasury shares” means — (a) shares that are held by the transferor company as treasury shares on the date of the offer; or (b) shares that become shares held by the transferor company as treasury shares after the date of the offer but before a date specified" (a "means" definition)

-- (1C)(b): "relevant treasury shares that cease to be held as treasury shares after the date of the offer are to be disregarded".
-- src:20653 | (b) relevant treasury shares that cease to be held as treasury
-- src:20654 | shares after the date of the offer are to be disregarded.
@ref s 215(1C)(b) (src:20653-20654)
GIVEN `the shares are relevant treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares cease to be held as treasury shares after the date of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1C)(b) the shares are to be disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the shares are relevant treasury shares` AND `the shares cease to be held as treasury shares after the date of the offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "relevant treasury shares that cease to be held as treasury shares after the date of the offer are to be disregarded" (shares outside this description are not addressed by the paragraph)

-- (1E): "To avoid doubt, where the requisite percentage ... has been reached, any subsequent issue of shares pursuant to the exercise of an option or right mentioned in subsection (1C)(a) does not affect (a) such approval;
-- (b) the transferee’s right to give a notice mentioned in subsection (1) after the approval; or (c) the validity of any such notice." A flat negative ("does not affect"): JUST FALSE for the three matters.
DECLARE `s 215(1E) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(1E)(a) the approval`
    `s 215(1E)(b) the transferee's right to give a notice mentioned in subsection (1) after the approval`
    `s 215(1E)(c) the validity of any such notice`
    `s 215(1E) some other matter`

-- src:20670 | (1E) To avoid doubt, where the requisite percentage in
-- src:20671 | subsection (1) of the total number of shares for the approval of an
-- src:20672 | offer in that subsection has been reached, any subsequent issue of
-- src:20673 | shares pursuant to the exercise of an option or right mentioned in
-- src:20674 | subsection (1C)(a) does not affect —
-- src:20676 | (a) such approval;
-- src:20681 | (b) the transferee’s right to give a notice mentioned in
-- src:20682 | subsection (1) after the approval; or
-- src:20684 | (c) the validity of any such notice.
@ref s 215(1E) (src:20670-20684)
GIVEN `the requisite percentage in subsection (1) of the total number of shares for the approval of an offer has been reached` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a subsequent issue of shares is pursuant to the exercise of an option or right mentioned in subsection (1C)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 215(1E) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1E) the subsequent issue of shares affects the matter` MEANS
    IF `the requisite percentage in subsection (1) of the total number of shares for the approval of an offer has been reached` AND `a subsequent issue of shares is pursuant to the exercise of an option or right mentioned in subsection (1C)(a)`
    THEN (CONSIDER matter
          WHEN `s 215(1E) some other matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not affect — (a) such approval; (b) the transferee’s right to give a notice ...; or (c) the validity of any such notice" (the subsection names three matters and says nothing of any other)
          OTHERWISE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any subsequent issue of shares pursuant to the exercise of an option or right mentioned in subsection (1C)(a) does not affect" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To avoid doubt, where the requisite percentage ... has been reached, any subsequent issue of shares pursuant to the exercise of an option or right mentioned in subsection (1C)(a)" (the subsection addresses only that issue after that percentage was reached)

§ `Section 215(2): the statement of names and addresses of the other dissenting shareholders`

-- (2): "Where a transferee has given notice to any dissenting shareholder ..., the dissenting shareholder is entitled to require the transferor company by a written demand served on the transferor company, within one month
-- from the date on which the notice was given, to supply the dissenting shareholder with a written statement of the names and addresses of all other dissenting shareholders as shown in the register of members".
-- An "entitled" function (fork F-215-7). Hohfeld: the shareholder's claim, the transferor company's duty (see the rule below).
-- src:20688 | (2) Where a transferee has given notice to any dissenting
-- src:20689 | shareholder that it desires to acquire the dissenting shareholder’s
-- src:20690 | shares, the dissenting shareholder is entitled to require the transferor
-- src:20691 | company by a written demand served on the transferor company,
-- src:20692 | within one month from the date on which the notice was given, to
-- src:20693 | supply the dissenting shareholder with a written statement of the
-- src:20694 | names and addresses of all other dissenting shareholders as shown in
-- src:20695 | the register of members, and the transferee is not entitled or bound to
@ref s 215(2) entitled (src:20688-20695)
GIVEN `the transferee has given notice under subsection (1) to the dissenting shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the day the written demand was served on the transferor company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(2) the dissenting shareholder is entitled to require the transferor company to supply the statement` MEANS
    IF NOT `the transferee has given notice under subsection (1) to the dissenting shareholder`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a transferee has given notice to any dissenting shareholder that it desires to acquire the dissenting shareholder’s shares, the dissenting shareholder is entitled" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))
    ELSE IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` `the day the written demand was served on the transferor company` 1 Months
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by a written demand served on the transferor company, within one month from the date on which the notice was given" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling (a))

-- (2): "the transferee is not entitled or bound to acquire the shares of the dissenting shareholders until 14 days after the posting of the statement of such names and addresses to the dissenting shareholder."
-- An "until" bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05): JUST TRUE until the last day of the 14 days, JUST FALSE after it. Where no statement was demanded the subsection sets no date: NOTHING (fork F-215-9, marginal reading for a lawyer).
-- src:20688 | (2) Where a transferee has given notice to any dissenting
-- src:20689 | shareholder that it desires to acquire the dissenting shareholder’s
-- src:20690 | shares, the dissenting shareholder is entitled to require the transferor
-- src:20691 | company by a written demand served on the transferor company,
-- src:20692 | within one month from the date on which the notice was given, to
-- src:20693 | supply the dissenting shareholder with a written statement of the
-- src:20694 | names and addresses of all other dissenting shareholders as shown in
-- src:20695 | the register of members, and the transferee is not entitled or bound to
-- src:20696 | acquire the shares of the dissenting shareholders until 14 days after
-- src:20697 | the posting of the statement of such names and addresses to the
-- src:20698 | dissenting shareholder.
@ref s 215(2) bar (src:20688-20698)
GIVEN `the transferee has given notice under subsection (1) to the dissenting shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dissenting shareholder has required the statement by a written demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the statement was posted to the dissenting shareholder, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(2) the transferee is not yet entitled or bound to acquire the shares` MEANS
    IF NOT `the transferee has given notice under subsection (1) to the dissenting shareholder`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a transferee has given notice to any dissenting shareholder" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))
    ELSE IF NOT `the dissenting shareholder has required the statement by a written demand`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection sets the bar by the posting of the statement and says nothing of a case in which no statement is demanded (fork F-215-9)
         ELSE CONSIDER `the day the statement was posted to the dissenting shareholder, if it was`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST d THEN
                  IF `the day asked about` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` d 14 Days)
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until 14 days after the posting of the statement" (an "until" bar: after the last day of the 14 days the bar is lifted; ruling (d) of 2026-11-05)

§ `Section 215(3) and (3A): the 90% reached by the transfers; the holder's right to require acquisition`

-- The counts for the 90% of subsection (3), as a witness could state them.
DECLARE `s 215(3) share count` HAS
    `s 215(3) the total number of the shares in the transferor company, or of the class, treasury shares included` IS A NUMBER
    `s 215(3) the number of shares transferred to the transferee or its nominee pursuant to the scheme or contract` IS A NUMBER
    `s 215(3) the number of other shares in the transferor company held by the transferee at the date of the transfer` IS A NUMBER
    `s 215(3A) the number of shares held by the transferor company as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER

-- (3A): "In subsection (3), for the purpose of calculating whether 90% of the total number of shares are held by the transferee, shares held by the transferor company as treasury shares are to be treated as having been acquired by the transferee."
-- The treasury shares are added where the 90% is measured against the total number of the shares, and not where it is measured against a class (the subsection speaks of "the total number of shares"; fork F-215-10).
-- src:20734 | (3A) In subsection (3), for the purpose of calculating whether
-- src:20735 | 90% of the total number of shares are held by the transferee, shares
-- src:20736 | held by the transferor company as treasury shares are to be treated as
-- src:20737 | having been acquired by the transferee.
@ref s 215(3A) (src:20734-20737)
GIVEN counts IS A `s 215(3) share count`
      `the 90% is measured against a class of the shares and not against the total number of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215(3A) the number of the treasury shares treated as having been acquired by the transferee` MEANS
    IF `the 90% is measured against a class of the shares and not against the total number of the shares`
    THEN 0
    ELSE counts's `s 215(3A) the number of shares held by the transferor company as treasury shares`

-- (3): "Where, pursuant to any such scheme or contract, shares in a transferor company are transferred to a transferee or its nominee and those shares together with any other shares in the transferor company held by the transferee
-- at the date of the transfer comprise or include 90% of the total number of the shares in the transferor company or of any class of those shares".
GIVEN counts IS A `s 215(3) share count`
      `the 90% is measured against a class of the shares and not against the total number of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215(3) the number of shares held by the transferee after the transfer, the treasury shares treated as acquired` MEANS
    ((counts's `s 215(3) the number of shares transferred to the transferee or its nominee pursuant to the scheme or contract`)
     PLUS (counts's `s 215(3) the number of other shares in the transferor company held by the transferee at the date of the transfer`))
    PLUS (`s 215(3A) the number of the treasury shares treated as having been acquired by the transferee` counts `the 90% is measured against a class of the shares and not against the total number of the shares`)

-- src:20702 | (3) Where, pursuant to any such scheme or contract, shares in a
-- src:20703 | transferor company are transferred to a transferee or its nominee and
-- src:20704 | those shares together with any other shares in the transferor company
-- src:20705 | held by the transferee at the date of the transfer comprise or include
-- src:20706 | 90% of the total number of the shares in the transferor company or of
-- src:20707 | any class of those shares, then —
@ref s 215(3) ninety per cent (src:20702-20707)
GIVEN counts IS A `s 215(3) share count`
      `the 90% is measured against a class of the shares and not against the total number of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(3) the shares transferred, together with the other shares held by the transferee, comprise or include 90%` MEANS
    IF    ((counts's `s 215(3) the total number of the shares in the transferor company, or of the class, treasury shares included`) GREATER THAN 0)
      AND (((`s 215(3) the number of shares held by the transferee after the transfer, the treasury shares treated as acquired` counts `the 90% is measured against a class of the shares and not against the total number of the shares`) TIMES 100)
           AT LEAST ((counts's `s 215(3) the total number of the shares in the transferor company, or of the class, treasury shares included`) TIMES 90))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... those shares together with any other shares in the transferor company held by the transferee at the date of the transfer comprise or include 90% of the total number of the shares" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b); fork F-215-10)

-- (3)(a): "then (a) the transferee must within one month from the date of the transfer (unless on a previous transfer pursuant to the scheme or contract it has already complied with this requirement) give notice of that fact in the prescribed
-- manner to the holders of the remaining shares or of the remaining shares of that class who have not assented to the scheme or contract".
-- src:20702 | (3) Where, pursuant to any such scheme or contract, shares in a
-- src:20703 | transferor company are transferred to a transferee or its nominee and
-- src:20704 | those shares together with any other shares in the transferor company
-- src:20705 | held by the transferee at the date of the transfer comprise or include
-- src:20706 | 90% of the total number of the shares in the transferor company or of
-- src:20707 | any class of those shares, then —
-- src:20709 | (a) the transferee must within one month from the date of the
-- src:20710 | transfer (unless on a previous transfer pursuant to the
-- src:20711 | scheme or contract it has already complied with this
-- src:20712 | requirement) give notice of that fact in the prescribed
-- src:20713 | manner to the holders of the remaining shares or of the
-- src:20714 | remaining shares of that class who have not assented to the
-- src:20715 | scheme or contract; and
@ref s 215(3)(a) (src:20702-20715)
GIVEN `the shares transferred, together with the other shares held by the transferee, comprise or include 90%` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferee has already complied with this requirement on a previous transfer pursuant to the scheme or contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(3)(a) the transferee must give notice of that fact to the holders of the remaining shares who have not assented` MEANS
    IF NOT `the shares transferred, together with the other shares held by the transferee, comprise or include 90%`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... comprise or include 90% ... then — (a) the transferee must" (a "where" condition on a duty; periods ruling (b), marginal reading (a))
    ELSE IF `the transferee has already complied with this requirement on a previous transfer pursuant to the scheme or contract`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(unless on a previous transfer pursuant to the scheme or contract it has already complied with this requirement)" (an "unless" once met; case-by-case, fork F-215-11)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 215(3)(a) period (src:20709-20715)
GIVEN `the day of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `the day the transferee gave the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(3)(a) the notice was given within one month from the date of the transfer` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the transfer` `the day the transferee gave the notice` 1 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the transferee must within one month from the date of the transfer ... give notice of that fact" (a duty with a stated period, not met; the provision's own question)

-- The number of days from a start day to the last day for the notice (for the trace of the duty below).
GIVEN `the day of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215(3)(a) the number of days from the start day to the last day for the notice` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the transfer` 1 Months) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

-- (3)(b): "any such holder may within 3 months from the giving of the notice to such holder require the transferee to acquire the shares in question". A power ("may") gated by a "where" and a period: JUST FALSE (fork F-215-12);
-- a holder who has assented is outside "any such holder" (NOTHING, periods ruling (c)); where no notice was given the period has not begun and the subsection is silent (NOTHING).
-- src:20702 | (3) Where, pursuant to any such scheme or contract, shares in a
-- src:20703 | transferor company are transferred to a transferee or its nominee and
-- src:20704 | those shares together with any other shares in the transferor company
-- src:20705 | held by the transferee at the date of the transfer comprise or include
-- src:20706 | 90% of the total number of the shares in the transferor company or of
-- src:20707 | any class of those shares, then —
-- src:20709 | (a) the transferee must within one month from the date of the
-- src:20710 | transfer (unless on a previous transfer pursuant to the
-- src:20711 | scheme or contract it has already complied with this
-- src:20712 | requirement) give notice of that fact in the prescribed
-- src:20713 | manner to the holders of the remaining shares or of the
-- src:20714 | remaining shares of that class who have not assented to the
-- src:20715 | scheme or contract; and
-- src:20717 | (b) any such holder may within 3 months from the giving of
-- src:20718 | the notice to such holder require the transferee to acquire
-- src:20719 | the shares in question,
@ref s 215(3)(b) (src:20702-20719)
GIVEN `the shares transferred, together with the other shares held by the transferee, comprise or include 90%` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder is a holder of the remaining shares who has not assented to the scheme or contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given to the holder, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the holder required the transferee to acquire the shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(3)(b) the holder may require the transferee to acquire the shares in question` MEANS
    IF NOT `the shares transferred, together with the other shares held by the transferee, comprise or include 90%`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... comprise or include 90% of the total number of the shares ..., then — ... (b) any such holder may" (split site (ii): a "where" gate on a power; periods ruling (b); fork F-215-12)
    ELSE IF NOT `the holder is a holder of the remaining shares who has not assented to the scheme or contract`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the holders of the remaining shares ... who have not assented to the scheme or contract; and (b) any such holder may" (a grant naming holders who have not assented; periods ruling (c))
         ELSE CONSIDER `the day the notice was given to the holder, if it was`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "within 3 months from the giving of the notice to such holder" (the period runs from the notice; the paragraph does not say what a holder may do where no notice was given)
              WHEN JUST d THEN
                  IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` d `the day the holder required the transferee to acquire the shares` 3 Months
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any such holder may within 3 months from the giving of the notice to such holder require" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling (a); fork F-215-12)

-- (3): "where a shareholder gives notice under paragraph (b) with respect to any shares, the transferee is entitled and bound to acquire those shares". An "entitled" function (fork F-215-7).
-- src:20721 | and where a shareholder gives notice under paragraph (b) with
-- src:20722 | respect to any shares, the transferee is entitled and bound to acquire
-- src:20723 | those shares on the terms on which under the scheme or contract the
@ref s 215(3) entitled (src:20721-20723)
GIVEN `a shareholder has given notice under paragraph (b) with respect to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(3) the transferee is entitled and bound to acquire the shares` MEANS
    IF `a shareholder has given notice under paragraph (b) with respect to the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a shareholder gives notice under paragraph (b) with respect to any shares, the transferee is entitled and bound to acquire those shares" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))

-- (3): "on the terms on which under the scheme or contract the shares of the approving shareholders were transferred to it, or on such other terms as are agreed or as the Court on the application of either the transferee
-- or the shareholder thinks fit to order". If other terms are agreed and the Court has ordered other terms, the text does not say which governs (NOTHING; fork F-215-13).
DECLARE `s 215(3) terms` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(3) the terms on which under the scheme or contract the shares of the approving shareholders were transferred to the transferee`
    `s 215(3) such other terms as are agreed`
    `s 215(3) such other terms as the Court thinks fit to order`

-- src:20721 | and where a shareholder gives notice under paragraph (b) with
-- src:20722 | respect to any shares, the transferee is entitled and bound to acquire
-- src:20723 | those shares on the terms on which under the scheme or contract the
-- src:20724 | shares of the approving shareholders were transferred to it, or on such
-- src:20729 | other terms as are agreed or as the Court on the application of either
-- src:20730 | the transferee or the shareholder thinks fit to order.
@ref s 215(3) terms (src:20721-20730)
GIVEN `other terms have been agreed between the transferee and the shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court, on the application of the transferee or the shareholder, has ordered other terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 215(3) terms`
`s 215(3) the terms on which the transferee must acquire the shares` MEANS
    IF `other terms have been agreed between the transferee and the shareholder` AND `the Court, on the application of the transferee or the shareholder, has ordered other terms`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "or on such other terms as are agreed or as the Court ... thinks fit to order" (the subsection does not rank agreed terms against terms ordered by the Court; fork F-215-13)
    ELSE IF `the Court, on the application of the transferee or the shareholder, has ordered other terms`
         THEN JUST `s 215(3) such other terms as the Court thinks fit to order`
         ELSE IF `other terms have been agreed between the transferee and the shareholder`
              THEN JUST `s 215(3) such other terms as are agreed`
              ELSE JUST `s 215(3) the terms on which under the scheme or contract the shares of the approving shareholders were transferred to the transferee`

§ `Section 215(4) to (7): the transfer, the trust, the Official Receiver`

-- (4): "Where a notice has been given by the transferee under subsection (1) and the Court has not, on an application made by the dissenting shareholder, ordered to the contrary, the transferee must ... (a) transmit a copy of the notice
-- to the transferor company together with an instrument of transfer ...; and (b) pay, allot or transfer to the transferor company the amount or other consideration".
-- src:20741 | (4) Where a notice has been given by the transferee under
-- src:20742 | subsection (1) and the Court has not, on an application made by
-- src:20743 | the dissenting shareholder, ordered to the contrary, the transferee
-- src:20744 | must, after the expiration of one month after the date on which the
-- src:20745 | notice has been given or, after 14 days after a statement has been
-- src:20746 | supplied to a dissenting shareholder pursuant to subsection (2) or if an
-- src:20747 | application to the Court by the dissenting shareholder is then pending,
-- src:20748 | after that application has been disposed of —
-- src:20750 | (a) transmit a copy of the notice to the transferor company
-- src:20751 | together with an instrument of transfer executed, on behalf
-- src:20752 | of the shareholder by any person appointed by the
-- src:20753 | transferee, and on its own behalf by the transferee; and
-- src:20755 | (b) pay, allot or transfer to the transferor company the amount
-- src:20756 | or other consideration representing the price payable by the
-- src:20757 | transferee for the shares which by virtue of this section the
-- src:20758 | transferee is entitled to acquire,
@ref s 215(4) (src:20741-20758)
GIVEN `a notice has been given by the transferee under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has, on an application made by the dissenting shareholder, ordered to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(4) the transferee must transmit a copy of the notice and pay, allot or transfer the consideration to the transferor company` MEANS
    IF `a notice has been given by the transferee under subsection (1)` AND (NOT `the Court has, on an application made by the dissenting shareholder, ordered to the contrary`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a notice has been given by the transferee under subsection (1) and the Court has not, on an application made by the dissenting shareholder, ordered to the contrary, the transferee must" (a "where" condition on a duty; periods ruling (b), marginal reading (a))

-- (4): the time of the duty: "after the expiration of one month after the date on which the notice has been given or, after 14 days after a statement has been supplied to a dissenting shareholder pursuant to subsection (2) or if an application
-- to the Court by the dissenting shareholder is then pending, after that application has been disposed of". The first day on which the duty is due: the day after the last day of the later period, or the day after the application
-- is disposed of if that is later. While the application is still pending the day is not yet known (NOTHING). "Then pending" is read as pending at the end of the later period (fork F-215-14).
@ref s 215(4) time (src:20744-20748)
GIVEN `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `an application to the Court by the dissenting shareholder is then pending` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day that application was disposed of, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 215(4) the first day on which the transferee must act` MEANS
    IF NOT `an application to the Court by the dissenting shareholder is then pending`
    THEN JUST ((`s 215(1) the last day of the later of the one month and the 14 days` `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was`) PLUS 1)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day that application was disposed of, if it has been`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "if an application to the Court by the dissenting shareholder is then pending, after that application has been disposed of" (the day cannot be named until the application is disposed of)
         WHEN JUST d THEN
             IF d GREATER THAN (`s 215(1) the last day of the later of the one month and the 14 days` `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was`)
             THEN JUST (d PLUS 1)
             ELSE JUST ((`s 215(1) the last day of the later of the one month and the 14 days` `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was`) PLUS 1)

-- (5): "Any sums received by the transferor company under this section must be paid into a separate bank account, and any such sums and any other consideration so received must be held by the transferor company in trust for the several
-- persons entitled to the shares". Duties of the transferor company, no time stated: paying the sums into a separate bank account takes the s 52 input, and holding them in trust (MAINTENANCE) has no deadline (see the rules below).
-- src:20765 | (5) Any sums received by the transferor company under this section
-- src:20766 | must be paid into a separate bank account, and any such sums and any
-- src:20767 | other consideration so received must be held by the transferor
-- src:20768 | company in trust for the several persons entitled to the shares in
-- src:20769 | respect of which they were respectively received.
@ref s 215(5) (src:20765-20769)
GIVEN `sums were received by the transferor company under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sums were paid into a separate bank account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(5) the transferor company has paid the sums into a separate bank account` MEANS
    IF NOT `sums were received by the transferor company under this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any sums received by the transferor company under this section must be paid into a separate bank account" (a duty arises only for sums received; the provision's own question)
    ELSE IF `the sums were paid into a separate bank account`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be paid into a separate bank account" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)

-- (6): "Where any money or other consideration is held in trust by a company for any person under this section, the company holding the money or other consideration may, after the expiration of 2 years and must before the expiration of 10 years
-- from the date on which the money or other consideration was received by the person, transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver." As in section 210(10A): after the 2 years, up to and including the last day of the 10 years.
-- "received by the person" is read as received by the company holding it (finding 3 in NOTES.md).
-- src:20773 | (6) Where any money or other consideration is held in trust by a
-- src:20774 | company for any person under this section, the company holding the
-- src:20775 | money or other consideration may, after the expiration of 2 years and
-- src:20776 | must before the expiration of 10 years from the date on which the
-- src:20781 | money or other consideration was received by the person, transfer the
-- src:20782 | money or other consideration to the Official Receiver.
@ref s 215(6) (src:20773-20782)
GIVEN `money or other consideration is held in trust by a company for a person under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the money or other consideration was received by the company holding it` IS A DATE
      `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(6) the transfer to the Official Receiver is within the time the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF NOT `money or other consideration is held in trust by a company for a person under this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any money or other consideration is held in trust by a company for any person under this section" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))
    ELSE IF `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the company holding it` 2 Years)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, after the expiration of 2 years" (a period the text fixes in its own words; a transfer on or before the last day of the 2 years is too early; periods ruling (a))
         ELSE IF `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the company holding it` 10 Years)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must before the expiration of 10 years from the date on which the money or other consideration was received" (a period the text fixes in its own words; a transfer after the last day of the 10 years is late; periods ruling (a))

-- The number of days from a start day to the last day of the 10 years (for the trace of the duty below).
GIVEN `the day the money or other consideration was received by the company holding it` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215(6) the number of days from the start day to the last day before the 10 years expire` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the company holding it` 10 Years) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

-- (7): "The Official Receiver must (a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (6) as if the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018; and
-- (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under subsection (6) in such manner as the Official Receiver thinks fit and must deal with the proceeds ... as if it were moneys paid ... under section 197".
DECLARE `s 215(7) treatment` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(7)(a) dealt with as if the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 215(7)(b) sold or disposed of in the manner the Official Receiver thinks fit, the proceeds dealt with as if moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`

-- src:20786 | (7) The Official Receiver must —
-- src:20788 | (a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (6) as if
-- src:20789 | the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under
-- src:20790 | section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:20791 | Dissolution Act 2018; and
-- src:20793 | (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under
-- src:20794 | subsection (6) in such manner as the Official Receiver
-- src:20795 | thinks fit and must deal with the proceeds of such sale or
-- src:20796 | disposal as if it were moneys paid to the Official Receiver
-- src:20797 | under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:20798 | Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 215(7) (src:20786-20798)
GIVEN `the thing received under subsection (6) is money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing received under subsection (6) is other consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 215(7) treatment`
`s 215(7) how the Official Receiver must deal with what is received under subsection (6)` MEANS
    IF `the thing received under subsection (6) is money`
    THEN JUST `s 215(7)(a) dealt with as if the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    ELSE IF `the thing received under subsection (6) is other consideration`
         THEN JUST `s 215(7)(b) sold or disposed of in the manner the Official Receiver thinks fit, the proceeds dealt with as if moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (6) ...; and (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under subsection (6)" (the subsection says what the Official Receiver does with money and with other consideration received under (6), and nothing of anything else)

§ `Section 215(8) to (8C): the words defined`

-- (8): "In this section, a dissenting shareholder includes a shareholder who has not assented to the scheme or contract and any shareholder who has failed or refused to transfer the shareholder’s shares to the transferee in accordance with the scheme or contract."
-- src:20802 | (8) In this section, a dissenting shareholder includes a shareholder
-- src:20803 | who has not assented to the scheme or contract and any shareholder
-- src:20804 | who has failed or refused to transfer the shareholder’s shares to the
-- src:20805 | transferee in accordance with the scheme or contract.
@ref s 215(8) (src:20802-20805)
GIVEN `the shareholder has not assented to the scheme or contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder has failed or refused to transfer the shareholder's shares to the transferee in accordance with the scheme or contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(8) the shareholder is a dissenting shareholder` MEANS
    IF `the shareholder has not assented to the scheme or contract` OR `the shareholder has failed or refused to transfer the shareholder's shares to the transferee in accordance with the scheme or contract`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a dissenting shareholder includes a shareholder who has not assented ... and any shareholder who has failed or refused to transfer" leaves the list open

-- (8A): "To avoid doubt, a reference in subsection (8) to a shareholder includes one whose shares are issued pursuant to the exercise of an option or right mentioned in subsection (1C)(a), after the offer ... has been approved".
-- src:20809 | (8A) To avoid doubt, a reference in subsection (8) to a shareholder
-- src:20810 | includes one whose shares are issued pursuant to the exercise of an
-- src:20811 | option or right mentioned in subsection (1C)(a), after the offer
-- src:20812 | mentioned in subsection (1) has been approved in accordance with
-- src:20813 | subsection (1).
@ref s 215(8A) (src:20809-20813)
GIVEN `the shareholder's shares are issued pursuant to the exercise of an option or right mentioned in subsection (1C)(a), after the offer mentioned in subsection (1) has been approved in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(8A) the shareholder is within the reference to a shareholder in subsection (8)` MEANS
    IF `the shareholder's shares are issued pursuant to the exercise of an option or right mentioned in subsection (1C)(a), after the offer mentioned in subsection (1) has been approved in accordance with subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference in subsection (8) to a shareholder includes one whose shares are issued pursuant to the exercise of an option or right" leaves the list open

-- (8AA): "In this section and sections 215AA and 215AB, “shares” includes units of shares." A unit is a unit of a share as s 4(1) "unit" defines it.
-- src:20817 | (8AA) In this section and sections 215AA and 215AB, “shares”
-- src:20818 | includes units of shares.
@ref s 215(8AA) (src:20817-20818)
GIVEN `the thing is a right or interest, whether legal or equitable, in a share, by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is an option to acquire any such right or interest in a share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(8AA) the thing is within the word shares` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "unit" the right or option is within the word unit` `the thing is a right or interest, whether legal or equitable, in a share, by whatever name called` `the thing is an option to acquire any such right or interest in a share` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“shares” includes units of shares" leaves the list open

-- (8AB): "In this section and section 215AB, “shareholders” includes holders of units of shares but does not include a person who holds units of shares only beneficially."
-- src:20822 | (8AB) In this section and section 215AB, “shareholders” includes
-- src:20823 | holders of units of shares but does not include a person who holds
-- src:20824 | units of shares only beneficially.
@ref s 215(8AB) (src:20822-20824)
GIVEN `the person holds units of shares only beneficially` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a holder of units of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(8AB) the person is within the word shareholders` MEANS
    IF `the person holds units of shares only beneficially`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“shareholders” includes holders of units of shares but does not include a person who holds units of shares only beneficially" (a flat negative)
    ELSE IF `the person is a holder of units of shares`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“shareholders” includes holders of units of shares" leaves the list open

-- (8AC): "In this section, “register of members” includes any records kept by or with respect to the transferor company of the names and addresses of holders of units of shares."
-- src:20828 | (8AC) In this section, “register of members” includes any records
-- src:20829 | kept by or with respect to the transferor company of the names and
-- src:20830 | addresses of holders of units of shares.
@ref s 215(8AC) (src:20828-20830)
GIVEN `the records are kept by or with respect to the transferor company of the names and addresses of holders of units of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(8AC) the records are within the register of members` MEANS
    IF `the records are kept by or with respect to the transferor company of the names and addresses of holders of units of shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“register of members” includes any records kept by or with respect to the transferor company" leaves the list open

-- (8B): "Nothing in the definition of “shares” in subsection (8AA) is to be read as requiring any securities to be treated — (a) as shares of the same class as those into which they are convertible or for which the holder is entitled to subscribe; or
-- (b) as shares of the same class as other securities by reason only that the shares into which they are convertible ... are of the same class." A flat negative.
DECLARE `s 215(8B) the treatment` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(8B)(a) treating securities as shares of the same class as those into which they are convertible or for which the holder is entitled to subscribe`
    `s 215(8B)(b) treating securities as shares of the same class as other securities by reason only that the shares into which they are convertible or for which the holder is entitled to subscribe are of the same class`
    `s 215(8B) some other treatment`

-- src:20837 | (8B) Nothing in the definition of “shares” in subsection (8AA) is to
-- src:20838 | be read as requiring any securities to be treated —
-- src:20840 | (a) as shares of the same class as those into which they are
-- src:20841 | convertible or for which the holder is entitled to subscribe;
-- src:20842 | or
-- src:20844 | (b) as shares of the same class as other securities by reason
-- src:20845 | only that the shares into which they are convertible or for
-- src:20846 | which the holder is entitled to subscribe are of the same
-- src:20847 | class.
@ref s 215(8B) (src:20837-20847)
GIVEN treatment IS A `s 215(8B) the treatment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(8B) the definition of shares requires the securities to be treated that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER treatment
    WHEN `s 215(8B) some other treatment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in the definition ... is to be read as requiring any securities to be treated — (a) ...; or (b) ..." (the subsection names two treatments and says nothing of any other)
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in the definition of “shares” in subsection (8AA) is to be read as requiring any securities to be treated" (a flat negative)

§ `Section 215(9) to (12): shares held or acquired by others; shares already held; shares acquired during the offer; control`

-- (9): "For the purposes of this section, shares held or acquired — (a) by a nominee on behalf of the transferee; or (b) by a related corporation of the transferee or by a nominee of that related corporation, are to be treated as held or acquired by the transferee."
-- "related corporation" is the keel's s 4(1) definition (a corporation deemed related by virtue of section 6).
DECLARE `s 215(9) who holds or acquires the shares` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(9)(a) a nominee on behalf of the transferee`
    `s 215(9)(b) a related corporation of the transferee`
    `s 215(9)(b) a nominee of a related corporation of the transferee`
    `s 215(9) someone else`

-- src:20853 | (9) For the purposes of this section, shares held or acquired —
-- src:20855 | (a) by a nominee on behalf of the transferee; or
-- src:20857 | (b) by a related corporation of the transferee or by a nominee
-- src:20858 | of that related corporation,
-- src:20860 | are to be treated as held or acquired by the transferee.
@ref s 215(9) (src:20853-20860)
GIVEN holder IS A `s 215(9) who holds or acquires the shares`
      `the corporation is deemed to be related to the transferee by virtue of section 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(9) the shares are to be treated as held or acquired by the transferee` MEANS
    CONSIDER holder
    WHEN `s 215(9)(a) a nominee on behalf of the transferee` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 215(9)(b) a related corporation of the transferee` THEN
        IF `s 4(1) "related corporation" the other corporation is a related corporation of the corporation` `the corporation is deemed to be related to the transferee by virtue of section 6` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by a related corporation of the transferee" (a corporation that is not deemed related by section 6 is outside the paragraph)
    WHEN `s 215(9)(b) a nominee of a related corporation of the transferee` THEN
        IF `s 4(1) "related corporation" the other corporation is a related corporation of the corporation` `the corporation is deemed to be related to the transferee by virtue of section 6` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "or by a nominee of that related corporation" (a nominee of a corporation that is not a related corporation is outside the paragraph)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shares held or acquired — (a) by a nominee on behalf of the transferee; or (b) by a related corporation of the transferee or by a nominee of that related corporation" (a deeming that names two holders and says nothing of any other)

-- (12): "For the purposes of subsection (9A)(d), a body corporate is controlled by a transferee or person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of subsection (9A) if (a) the transferee or person ... is entitled to exercise or control the
-- exercise of not less than 50% of the voting power in the body corporate or such percentage of the voting power ... as may be prescribed, whichever is lower; or (b) the body corporate is, or a majority of its directors are, accustomed or
-- under an obligation whether formal or informal to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the transferee or the person".
DECLARE `s 215(12) control facts` HAS
    `s 215(12)(a) the percentage of the voting power in the body corporate the transferee or person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of` IS A NUMBER
    `s 215(12)(a) the percentage of the voting power prescribed, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 215(12)(b) the body corporate is, or a majority of its directors are, accustomed or under an obligation whether formal or informal to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the transferee or the person` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:20927 | (a) the transferee or person (as the case may be) is entitled to
-- src:20928 | exercise or control the exercise of not less than 50% of the
-- src:20929 | voting power in the body corporate or such percentage of
-- src:20934 | the voting power in the body corporate as may be
-- src:20935 | prescribed, whichever is lower; or
@ref s 215(12)(a) (src:20927-20935)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 215(12) control facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215(12)(a) the voting power reaches the lower of 50% and the prescribed percentage` MEANS
    CONSIDER (facts's `s 215(12)(a) the percentage of the voting power prescribed, if any`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN (facts's `s 215(12)(a) the percentage of the voting power in the body corporate the transferee or person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of`) AT LEAST 50
    WHEN JUST p THEN (facts's `s 215(12)(a) the percentage of the voting power in the body corporate the transferee or person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of`) AT LEAST (IF p LESS THAN 50 THEN p ELSE 50)

-- src:20923 | (12) For the purposes of subsection (9A)(d), a body corporate is
-- src:20924 | controlled by a transferee or person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or
-- src:20925 | (c) of subsection (9A) if —
-- src:20927 | (a) the transferee or person (as the case may be) is entitled to
-- src:20928 | exercise or control the exercise of not less than 50% of the
-- src:20929 | voting power in the body corporate or such percentage of
-- src:20934 | the voting power in the body corporate as may be
-- src:20935 | prescribed, whichever is lower; or
-- src:20937 | (b) the body corporate is, or a majority of its directors are,
-- src:20938 | accustomed or under an obligation whether formal or
-- src:20939 | informal to act in accordance with the directions,
-- src:20940 | instructions or wishes of the transferee or the person (as
-- src:20941 | the case may be).
@ref s 215(12) (src:20923-20941)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 215(12) control facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(12) the body corporate is controlled by the transferee or the person` MEANS
    IF    `s 215(12)(a) the voting power reaches the lower of 50% and the prescribed percentage` facts
       OR (facts's `s 215(12)(b) the body corporate is, or a majority of its directors are, accustomed or under an obligation whether formal or informal to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the transferee or the person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a body corporate is controlled by a transferee or person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of subsection (9A) if —" (a condition introduced by "if", not met; marginal reading (a))

-- (9A): "In addition to subsection (9), in respect of an offer made on or after the date of commencement of section 10(a) of the Companies, Business Trusts and Other Bodies (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2023, shares held or acquired — (a) by a person who
-- is accustomed or is under an obligation ... to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the transferee ...; (b) by the transferee’s spouse, parent, brother, sister, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter
-- or stepdaughter; (c) by a person whose directions, instructions or wishes the transferee is accustomed or is under an obligation ... to act in accordance with ...; or (d) by a body corporate that is controlled (within the meaning of
-- subsection (12)) by the transferee or a person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c), are also to be treated as held or acquired by the transferee."
DECLARE `s 215(9A) who holds or acquires the shares` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(9A)(a) a person who is accustomed or under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the transferee in respect of the transferor company`
    `s 215(9A)(b) the transferee's spouse, parent, brother, sister, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or stepdaughter`
    `s 215(9A)(c) a person whose directions, instructions or wishes the transferee is accustomed or under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in accordance with, in respect of the transferor company`
    `s 215(9A)(d) a body corporate controlled by the transferee or by a person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`
    `s 215(9A) someone else`

-- src:20864 | (9A) In addition to subsection (9), in respect of an offer made on or
-- src:20865 | after the date of commencement of section 10(a) of the Companies,
-- src:20866 | Business Trusts and Other Bodies (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act
-- src:20867 | 2023, shares held or acquired —
-- src:20869 | (a) by a person who is accustomed or is under an obligation
-- src:20870 | whether formal or informal to act in accordance with the
-- src:20871 | directions, instructions or wishes of the transferee in
-- src:20872 | respect of the transferor company;
-- src:20874 | (b) by the transferee’s spouse, parent, brother, sister, son,
-- src:20875 | adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or
-- src:20876 | stepdaughter;
-- src:20878 | (c) by a person whose directions, instructions or wishes the
-- src:20879 | transferee is accustomed or is under an obligation whether
-- src:20880 | formal or informal to act in accordance with, in respect of
-- src:20881 | the transferor company; or
-- src:20886 | (d) by a body corporate that is controlled (within the meaning
-- src:20887 | of subsection (12)) by the transferee or a person mentioned
-- src:20888 | in paragraph (a), (b) or (c),
-- src:20890 | are also to be treated as held or acquired by the transferee.
@ref s 215(9A) (src:20864-20890)
GIVEN `the offer was made on or after the date of commencement of section 10(a) of the Companies, Business Trusts and Other Bodies (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
      holder IS A `s 215(9A) who holds or acquires the shares`
      facts IS A `s 215(12) control facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(9A) the shares are also to be treated as held or acquired by the transferee` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offer was made on or after the date of commencement of section 10(a) of the Companies, Business Trusts and Other Bodies (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2023`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an offer made on or after the date of commencement of section 10(a) of the Companies, Business Trusts and Other Bodies (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2023" (the subsection speaks of those offers and says nothing of an earlier one; periods ruling (c))
    ELSE CONSIDER holder
         WHEN `s 215(9A)(a) a person who is accustomed or under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the transferee in respect of the transferor company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 215(9A)(b) the transferee's spouse, parent, brother, sister, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or stepdaughter` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 215(9A)(c) a person whose directions, instructions or wishes the transferee is accustomed or under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in accordance with, in respect of the transferor company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 215(9A)(d) a body corporate controlled by the transferee or by a person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` THEN
             IF `s 215(12) the body corporate is controlled by the transferee or the person` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by a body corporate that is controlled (within the meaning of subsection (12))" (a body corporate that is not so controlled is outside the paragraph)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shares held or acquired — (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; or (d) ... are also to be treated as held or acquired by the transferee" (a deeming over four listed holders and no other)

-- (10): "The reference in subsection (1) to shares already held by the transferee includes a reference to shares which the transferee has contracted to acquire but is not to be construed as including shares which are the subject of a contract
-- binding the holder thereof to accept the offer when it is made, being a contract entered into by the holder for no consideration and under seal or for no consideration other than a promise by the transferee to make the offer."
-- src:20894 | (10) The reference in subsection (1) to shares already held by the
-- src:20895 | transferee includes a reference to shares which the transferee has
-- src:20896 | contracted to acquire but is not to be construed as including shares
-- src:20897 | which are the subject of a contract binding the holder thereof to
-- src:20898 | accept the offer when it is made, being a contract entered into by the
-- src:20899 | holder for no consideration and under seal or for no consideration
-- src:20900 | other than a promise by the transferee to make the offer.
@ref s 215(10) (src:20894-20900)
GIVEN `the shares are held by the transferee at the date of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferee has contracted to acquire the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are the subject of a contract binding the holder to accept the offer when it is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that contract was entered into by the holder for no consideration and under seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that contract was entered into by the holder for no consideration other than a promise by the transferee to make the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(10) the shares are shares already held by the transferee within subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the shares are the subject of a contract binding the holder to accept the offer when it is made` AND (`that contract was entered into by the holder for no consideration and under seal` OR `that contract was entered into by the holder for no consideration other than a promise by the transferee to make the offer`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not to be construed as including shares which are the subject of a contract binding the holder thereof to accept the offer when it is made, being a contract entered into by the holder for no consideration and under seal or for no consideration other than a promise by the transferee to make the offer" (a flat negative)
    ELSE IF `the shares are held by the transferee at the date of the offer` OR `the transferee has contracted to acquire the shares`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "shares already held by the transferee includes a reference to shares which the transferee has contracted to acquire" leaves the list open

-- (11): "Where, during the period within which an offer for the transfer of shares to the transferee can be approved, the transferee acquires or contracts to acquire any of the shares whose transfer is involved but otherwise than by virtue of the approval
-- of the offer, then, if — (a) the consideration for which the shares are acquired or contracted to be acquired (called in this subsection the acquisition consideration) does not at that time exceed the consideration specified in the terms of the offer;
-- or (b) those terms are subsequently revised so that when the revision is announced the acquisition consideration, at the time referred to in paragraph (a), no longer exceeds the consideration specified in those terms, the transferee is to be treated ...
-- as having acquired or contracted to acquire those shares by virtue of the approval of the offer."
-- src:20904 | (11) Where, during the period within which an offer for the transfer
-- src:20905 | of shares to the transferee can be approved, the transferee acquires or
-- src:20906 | contracts to acquire any of the shares whose transfer is involved but
-- src:20907 | otherwise than by virtue of the approval of the offer, then, if —
-- src:20909 | (a) the consideration for which the shares are acquired or
-- src:20910 | contracted to be acquired (called in this subsection the
-- src:20911 | acquisition consideration) does not at that time exceed the
-- src:20912 | consideration specified in the terms of the offer; or
-- src:20914 | (b) those terms are subsequently revised so that when the
-- src:20915 | revision is announced the acquisition consideration, at the
-- src:20916 | time referred to in paragraph (a), no longer exceeds the
-- src:20917 | consideration specified in those terms,
-- src:20919 | the transferee is to be treated for the purposes of this section as having
-- src:20920 | acquired or contracted to acquire those shares by virtue of the
-- src:20921 | approval of the offer.
@ref s 215(11) (src:20904-20921)
GIVEN `during the period within which an offer for the transfer of shares to the transferee can be approved, the transferee acquires or contracts to acquire shares whose transfer is involved, otherwise than by virtue of the approval of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acquisition consideration` IS A NUMBER
      `the consideration specified in the terms of the offer at that time` IS A NUMBER
      `the terms of the offer are subsequently revised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration specified in the revised terms when the revision is announced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(11) the transferee is to be treated as having acquired the shares by virtue of the approval of the offer` MEANS
    IF NOT `during the period within which an offer for the transfer of shares to the transferee can be approved, the transferee acquires or contracts to acquire shares whose transfer is involved, otherwise than by virtue of the approval of the offer`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, during the period within which an offer for the transfer of shares to the transferee can be approved, the transferee acquires or contracts to acquire any of the shares whose transfer is involved but otherwise than by virtue of the approval of the offer" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))
    ELSE IF    `the acquisition consideration` AT MOST `the consideration specified in the terms of the offer at that time`
            OR (`the terms of the offer are subsequently revised` AND (`the acquisition consideration` AT MOST `the consideration specified in the revised terms when the revision is announced`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then, if — (a) the consideration ... does not at that time exceed the consideration specified in the terms of the offer; or (b) those terms are subsequently revised so that ... no longer exceeds" (a condition introduced by "if", not met; marginal reading (a))

§ `Section 215AA: joint offers`

-- Heading (line 20947): "Joint offers": not operative.

-- (1): "In the case of a scheme involving an offer to acquire all of the shares in a company, or all of the shares in any particular class in a company, by 2 or more persons jointly (called in this section the joint transferees),
-- section 215 is to be read subject to this section."
-- src:20949 | 215AA.—(1) In the case of a scheme involving an offer to acquire
-- src:20950 | all of the shares in a company, or all of the shares in any particular
-- src:20951 | class in a company, by 2 or more persons jointly (called in this section
-- src:20952 | the joint transferees), section 215 is to be read subject to this section.
@ref s 215AA(1) (src:20949-20952)
GIVEN `the scheme involves an offer to acquire all of the shares in a company, or all of the shares in a particular class in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons making the offer jointly` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215AA(1) section 215 is to be read subject to section 215AA` MEANS
    IF `the scheme involves an offer to acquire all of the shares in a company, or all of the shares in a particular class in a company` AND (`the number of persons making the offer jointly` AT LEAST 2)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a scheme involving an offer to acquire all of the shares in a company, or all of the shares in any particular class in a company, by 2 or more persons jointly" (a "where"-type condition; periods ruling (b))

-- (2) and (3): the way in which the joint transferees satisfy the conditions for the rights under section 215(1) and (3).
DECLARE `s 215AA the way the shares were acquired` IS ONE OF
    `s 215AA(2)(a) by virtue of acceptances of the offer`
    `s 215AA(2)(b) in other cases`

-- (2): "The conditions for the exercise of the rights conferred by section 215(1) are satisfied (a) in the case of acquisitions of shares by virtue of acceptances of the offer — by the joint transferees acquiring or unconditionally
-- contracting to acquire the necessary shares jointly; or (b) in other cases — by the joint transferees acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the necessary shares either jointly or separately."
-- The text says how the conditions are satisfied and does not say "only": where the acceptances were acquired separately it is silent (NOTHING; fork F-215AA-1).
-- src:20956 | (2) The conditions for the exercise of the rights conferred by
-- src:20957 | section 215(1) are satisfied —
-- src:20959 | (a) in the case of acquisitions of shares by virtue of
-- src:20960 | acceptances of the offer — by the joint transferees
-- src:20961 | acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the
-- src:20962 | necessary shares jointly; or
-- src:20964 | (b) in other cases — by the joint transferees acquiring or
-- src:20965 | unconditionally contracting to acquire the necessary shares
-- src:20966 | either jointly or separately.
@ref s 215AA(2) (src:20956-20966)
GIVEN way IS A `s 215AA the way the shares were acquired`
      `the joint transferees acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire the necessary shares jointly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the joint transferees acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire the necessary shares separately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215AA(2) the conditions for the exercise of the rights conferred by section 215(1) are satisfied` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `s 215AA(2)(a) by virtue of acceptances of the offer` THEN
        IF `the joint transferees acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire the necessary shares jointly`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) in the case of acquisitions of shares by virtue of acceptances of the offer — by the joint transferees acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the necessary shares jointly" (the paragraph says how the conditions are satisfied and does not say that no other way will do; fork F-215AA-1)
    WHEN `s 215AA(2)(b) in other cases` THEN
        IF `the joint transferees acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire the necessary shares jointly` OR `the joint transferees acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire the necessary shares separately`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) in other cases — by the joint transferees acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the necessary shares either jointly or separately" (the paragraph says how the conditions are satisfied and does not say that no other way will do)

-- (3): "The conditions for the exercise of the rights conferred by section 215(3) are satisfied (a) ... by the joint transferees acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the necessary shares jointly; or
-- (b) in other cases — by the joint transferees acquiring or contracting (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met) to acquire the necessary shares either jointly or separately."
-- src:20970 | (3) The conditions for the exercise of the rights conferred by
-- src:20971 | section 215(3) are satisfied —
-- src:20973 | (a) in the case of acquisitions of shares by virtue of
-- src:20974 | acceptances of the offer — by the joint transferees
-- src:20975 | acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the
-- src:20976 | necessary shares jointly; or
-- src:20978 | (b) in other cases — by the joint transferees acquiring or
-- src:20979 | contracting (whether unconditionally or subject to
-- src:20984 | conditions being met) to acquire the necessary shares
-- src:20985 | either jointly or separately.
@ref s 215AA(3) (src:20970-20985)
GIVEN way IS A `s 215AA the way the shares were acquired`
      `the joint transferees acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire the necessary shares jointly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the joint transferees acquired, or contracted (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met) to acquire, the necessary shares either jointly or separately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215AA(3) the conditions for the exercise of the rights conferred by section 215(3) are satisfied` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `s 215AA(2)(a) by virtue of acceptances of the offer` THEN
        IF `the joint transferees acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire the necessary shares jointly`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) in the case of acquisitions of shares by virtue of acceptances of the offer — by the joint transferees acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the necessary shares jointly" (the paragraph says how the conditions are satisfied and does not say that no other way will do; fork F-215AA-1)
    WHEN `s 215AA(2)(b) in other cases` THEN
        IF `the joint transferees acquired, or contracted (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met) to acquire, the necessary shares either jointly or separately`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) in other cases — by the joint transferees acquiring or contracting (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met) to acquire the necessary shares either jointly or separately" (the paragraph says how the conditions are satisfied and does not say that no other way will do)

-- (4): "Subject to this section, the rights and obligations of the transferee under section 215 are respectively joint rights and joint and several obligations of the joint transferees."
DECLARE `s 215AA(4) what the transferee has under section 215` IS ONE OF
    `s 215AA(4) a right of the transferee under section 215`
    `s 215AA(4) an obligation of the transferee under section 215`

DECLARE `s 215AA(4) how the joint transferees hold it` IS ONE OF
    `s 215AA(4) a joint right of the joint transferees`
    `s 215AA(4) a joint and several obligation of the joint transferees`

-- src:20989 | (4) Subject to this section, the rights and obligations of the
-- src:20990 | transferee under section 215 are respectively joint rights and joint
-- src:20991 | and several obligations of the joint transferees.
@ref s 215AA(4) (src:20989-20991)
GIVEN what IS A `s 215AA(4) what the transferee has under section 215`
GIVETH A `s 215AA(4) how the joint transferees hold it`
`s 215AA(4) how the joint transferees hold what section 215 gives the transferee` MEANS
    CONSIDER what
    WHEN `s 215AA(4) a right of the transferee under section 215` THEN `s 215AA(4) a joint right of the joint transferees`
    WHEN `s 215AA(4) an obligation of the transferee under section 215` THEN `s 215AA(4) a joint and several obligation of the joint transferees`

-- (6): "The notice required to be given by the joint transferees under section 215(1) and (3) must be made by all of the joint transferees and, where one or more of them is a company, signed by a director of that company."
-- src:21001 | (6) The notice required to be given by the joint transferees under
-- src:21002 | section 215(1) and (3) must be made by all of the joint transferees
-- src:21003 | and, where one or more of them is a company, signed by a director of
-- src:21004 | that company.
@ref s 215AA(6) (src:21001-21004)
GIVEN `the notice is made by all of the joint transferees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every joint transferee that is a company has had the notice signed by a director of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215AA(6) the notice is made as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice is made by all of the joint transferees` AND `every joint transferee that is a company has had the notice signed by a director of that company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made by all of the joint transferees and, where one or more of them is a company, signed by a director of that company" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)

-- (5): "Subject to subsection (6), any notice or other document given or sent by or to the joint transferees under section 215 is complied with if the notice or document is given or sent by or to any of them."
-- A notice that subsection (6) governs is outside this subsection: NOTHING.
-- src:20995 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), any notice or other document given or
-- src:20996 | sent by or to the joint transferees under section 215 is complied with if
-- src:20997 | the notice or document is given or sent by or to any of them.
@ref s 215AA(5) (src:20995-20997)
GIVEN `the notice is one that subsection (6) requires to be made by all of the joint transferees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice or document is given or sent by or to any of the joint transferees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215AA(5) the notice or document is complied with` MEANS
    IF `the notice is one that subsection (6) requires to be made by all of the joint transferees`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the subsection): "Subject to subsection (6)" (subsection (6) decides the notices under section 215(1) and (3); this subsection does not)
    ELSE IF `the notice or document is given or sent by or to any of the joint transferees`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is complied with if the notice or document is given or sent by or to any of them" (a condition introduced by "if", not met; marginal reading (a))

§ `Section 215AB: the effect of the impossibility of communicating or accepting an offer`

-- Heading (lines 21008-21009): "Effect of impossibility, etc., of communicating or accepting offer made under scheme or contract": not operative.

-- (1): "Where there are holders of shares in a company to whom an offer to acquire shares in the company is not communicated, that does not prevent the offer from being an offer made under a scheme or contract for the purposes of section 215
-- if (a) those shareholders have no address in Singapore registered with the company; (b) the offer was not communicated to those shareholders (i) in order not to contravene the law of a country or territory outside Singapore; or (ii) because
-- communication to those shareholders would in the circumstances be unduly onerous; and (c) either (i) the offer is published in the Gazette; or (ii) the offer can be inspected, or a copy of it obtained, at a place in Singapore or on a website,
-- and a notice is published in the Gazette specifying the address of that place or website."
-- When a condition is not met, subsection (3)(a) says it is "not to be inferred" that the offer cannot be an offer made under a scheme: so the unmet "if" answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (fork F-215AB-1).
-- src:21011 | 215AB.—(1) Where there are holders of shares in a company to
-- src:21012 | whom an offer to acquire shares in the company is not communicated,
-- src:21013 | that does not prevent the offer from being an offer made under a
-- src:21014 | scheme or contract for the purposes of section 215 if —
-- src:21016 | (a) those shareholders have no address in Singapore registered
-- src:21017 | with the company;
-- src:21019 | (b) the offer was not communicated to those shareholders —
-- src:21021 | (i) in order not to contravene the law of a country or
-- src:21022 | territory outside Singapore; or
-- src:21024 | (ii) because communication to those shareholders would
-- src:21025 | in the circumstances be unduly onerous; and
-- src:21027 | (c) either —
-- src:21029 | (i) the offer is published in the Gazette; or
-- src:21031 | (ii) the offer can be inspected, or a copy of it obtained, at
-- src:21032 | a place in Singapore or on a website, and a notice is
-- src:21037 | published in the Gazette specifying the address of
-- src:21038 | that place or website.
-- src:21042 | (2) Where an offer is made to acquire shares in a company and there
-- src:21043 | are persons for whom, by reason of the law of a country or territory
-- src:21044 | outside Singapore, it is impossible to accept the offer, or more
-- src:21045 | difficult to do so, that does not prevent the offer from being made
-- src:21046 | under a scheme or contract for the purposes of section 215.
-- src:21050 | (3) It is not to be inferred —
-- src:21052 | (a) that an offer which is not communicated to every holder of
-- src:21053 | shares in the company cannot be an offer made under a
-- src:21054 | scheme or contract for the purposes of section 215 unless
-- src:21055 | the requirements of subsection (1)(a), (b) and (c) are met;
-- src:21056 | or
-- src:21058 | (b) that an offer which is impossible, or more difficult, for
-- src:21059 | certain persons to accept cannot be an offer made under a
-- src:21060 | scheme or contract for those purposes unless the reason for
-- src:21061 | the impossibility or difficulty is the reason mentioned in
-- src:21062 | subsection (2).
@ref s 215AB(1) (src:21011-21062)
GIVEN `there are holders of shares in the company to whom an offer to acquire shares in the company is not communicated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those shareholders have no address in Singapore registered with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer was not communicated in order not to contravene the law of a country or territory outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer was not communicated because communication to those shareholders would in the circumstances be unduly onerous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer can be inspected, or a copy of it obtained, at a place in Singapore or on a website, and a notice is published in the Gazette specifying the address of that place or website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215AB(1) the non-communication of the offer does not prevent it from being an offer made under a scheme or contract` MEANS
    IF NOT `there are holders of shares in the company to whom an offer to acquire shares in the company is not communicated`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there are holders of shares in a company to whom an offer to acquire shares in the company is not communicated" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b); fork F-215AB-1)
    ELSE IF    `those shareholders have no address in Singapore registered with the company`
           AND (`the offer was not communicated in order not to contravene the law of a country or territory outside Singapore` OR `the offer was not communicated because communication to those shareholders would in the circumstances be unduly onerous`)
           AND (`the offer is published in the Gazette` OR `the offer can be inspected, or a copy of it obtained, at a place in Singapore or on a website, and a notice is published in the Gazette specifying the address of that place or website`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that does not prevent the offer from being an offer made under a scheme or contract for the purposes of section 215 if —" read with subsection (3)(a): "It is not to be inferred — (a) that an offer which is not communicated to every holder of shares in the company cannot be an offer made under a scheme or contract ... unless the requirements of subsection (1)(a), (b) and (c) are met" (fork F-215AB-1)

-- (2): "Where an offer is made to acquire shares in a company and there are persons for whom, by reason of the law of a country or territory outside Singapore, it is impossible to accept the offer, or more difficult to do so,
-- that does not prevent the offer from being made under a scheme or contract for the purposes of section 215."
-- src:21042 | (2) Where an offer is made to acquire shares in a company and there
-- src:21043 | are persons for whom, by reason of the law of a country or territory
-- src:21044 | outside Singapore, it is impossible to accept the offer, or more
-- src:21045 | difficult to do so, that does not prevent the offer from being made
-- src:21046 | under a scheme or contract for the purposes of section 215.
@ref s 215AB(2) (src:21042-21046)
GIVEN `an offer is made to acquire shares in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are persons for whom, by reason of the law of a country or territory outside Singapore, it is impossible to accept the offer, or more difficult to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215AB(2) the impossibility or difficulty of accepting the offer does not prevent it from being made under a scheme or contract` MEANS
    IF `an offer is made to acquire shares in a company` AND `there are persons for whom, by reason of the law of a country or territory outside Singapore, it is impossible to accept the offer, or more difficult to do so`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offer is made to acquire shares in a company and there are persons for whom, by reason of the law of a country or territory outside Singapore, it is impossible to accept the offer, or more difficult to do so" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))

-- (3): "It is not to be inferred — (a) that an offer which is not communicated to every holder of shares in the company cannot be an offer made under a scheme or contract for the purposes of section 215 unless the requirements of subsection (1)(a), (b)
-- and (c) are met; or (b) that an offer which is impossible, or more difficult, for certain persons to accept cannot be an offer made under a scheme or contract for those purposes unless the reason for the impossibility or difficulty is the reason mentioned in subsection (2)."
-- A flat negative on an inference: JUST FALSE that it is to be inferred, where the case is the one the paragraph describes; NOTHING outside it.
-- src:21050 | (3) It is not to be inferred —
-- src:21052 | (a) that an offer which is not communicated to every holder of
-- src:21053 | shares in the company cannot be an offer made under a
-- src:21054 | scheme or contract for the purposes of section 215 unless
-- src:21055 | the requirements of subsection (1)(a), (b) and (c) are met;
-- src:21056 | or
-- src:21058 | (b) that an offer which is impossible, or more difficult, for
-- src:21059 | certain persons to accept cannot be an offer made under a
-- src:21060 | scheme or contract for those purposes unless the reason for
-- src:21061 | the impossibility or difficulty is the reason mentioned in
-- src:21062 | subsection (2).
@ref s 215AB(3)(a) (src:21050-21062)
GIVEN `the offer is not communicated to every holder of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215AB(3)(a) it is to be inferred that the offer cannot be an offer made under a scheme or contract unless the requirements of subsection (1)(a), (b) and (c) are met` MEANS
    IF `the offer is not communicated to every holder of shares in the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not to be inferred — (a) that an offer which is not communicated to every holder of shares in the company cannot be an offer made under a scheme or contract for the purposes of section 215 unless the requirements of subsection (1)(a), (b) and (c) are met" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offer which is not communicated to every holder of shares in the company" (the paragraph speaks of an offer not so communicated and says nothing of an offer that was)

@ref s 215AB(3)(b) (src:21058-21062)
GIVEN `the offer is impossible, or more difficult, for certain persons to accept` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215AB(3)(b) it is to be inferred that the offer cannot be an offer made under a scheme or contract unless the reason is the reason mentioned in subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the offer is impossible, or more difficult, for certain persons to accept`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) that an offer which is impossible, or more difficult, for certain persons to accept cannot be an offer made under a scheme or contract for those purposes unless the reason for the impossibility or difficulty is the reason mentioned in subsection (2)" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offer which is impossible, or more difficult, for certain persons to accept" (the paragraph speaks of such an offer and says nothing of any other)

§ `Regulative rules: the duties of ss 215 to 215AB that name a party and an act`

-- The acts the duties below are about. The Official Receiver's own acts are in the second type; its party is `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver` (sgd-compromise.l4).
DECLARE `s 215 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(1B) state which of the alternative terms is to apply where the dissenting shareholder fails to elect in time`
    `s 215(2) supply the dissenting shareholder with a written statement of the names and addresses of all other dissenting shareholders`
    `s 215(3)(a) give notice of the 90% to the holders of the remaining shares who have not assented`
    `s 215(4)(a) transmit a copy of the notice to the transferor company with an instrument of transfer`
    `s 215(4)(b) pay, allot or transfer to the transferor company the amount or other consideration`
    `s 215(4) register the transferee as the holder of the shares`
    `s 215(5) pay the sums received into a separate bank account`
    `s 215(5) hold the sums and other consideration in trust for the persons entitled`
    `s 215(6) transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver`
    `s 215AA(6) make the notice by all of the joint transferees, signed for each company by a director of that company`

DECLARE `s 215(7) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(7)(a) deal with the moneys received under subsection (6) as if they were paid under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 215(7)(b) sell or dispose of the other consideration and deal with the proceeds as if they were moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`

-- (1B): no time limit: no breach path.
-- src:20635 | (1B) In offering alternative terms to the shareholders, the transferee
-- src:20636 | must state which of those terms is to apply to the acquisition of the
-- src:20637 | shares of a dissenting shareholder where the dissenting shareholder
-- src:20638 | fails to make the election within the time allowed under
-- src:20639 | subsection (1A).
@ref s 215(1B) rule (src:20635-20639)
GIVEN who IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 act`
`s 215(1B) the transferee must state which of the alternative terms is to apply on a failure to elect` MEANS
    PARTY who
    MUST `s 215(1B) state which of the alternative terms is to apply where the dissenting shareholder fails to elect in time`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 215(1B) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY who BECAUSE "the offer did not state which of the alternative terms is to apply where the dissenting shareholder fails to elect in time" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- (2): the transferor company must supply the statement. No time stated: the time allowed is the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found` (notes/lest-without-deadline.md), so a late act reaches BREACH.
-- src:20688 | (2) Where a transferee has given notice to any dissenting
-- src:20689 | shareholder that it desires to acquire the dissenting shareholder’s
-- src:20690 | shares, the dissenting shareholder is entitled to require the transferor
-- src:20691 | company by a written demand served on the transferor company,
-- src:20692 | within one month from the date on which the notice was given, to
-- src:20693 | supply the dissenting shareholder with a written statement of the
-- src:20694 | names and addresses of all other dissenting shareholders as shown in
@ref s 215(2) rule (src:20688-20694)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 act`
`s 215(2) the transferor company must supply the dissenting shareholder with the written statement` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 215(2) supply the dissenting shareholder with a written statement of the names and addresses of all other dissenting shareholders`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the dissenting shareholder was not supplied with a written statement of the names and addresses of all other dissenting shareholders"

-- (3)(a): the transferee must give notice within one month from the date of the transfer: a deadline.
-- src:20709 | (a) the transferee must within one month from the date of the
-- src:20710 | transfer (unless on a previous transfer pursuant to the
-- src:20711 | scheme or contract it has already complied with this
-- src:20712 | requirement) give notice of that fact in the prescribed
-- src:20713 | manner to the holders of the remaining shares or of the
-- src:20714 | remaining shares of that class who have not assented to the
-- src:20715 | scheme or contract; and
@ref s 215(3)(a) rule (src:20709-20715)
GIVEN who IS A Party
      `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day for the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 act`
`s 215(3)(a) the transferee must give notice of the 90% within one month from the date of the transfer` MEANS
    PARTY who
    MUST `s 215(3)(a) give notice of the 90% to the holders of the remaining shares who have not assented`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day for the notice`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY who BECAUSE "notice of the 90% was not given within one month from the date of the transfer"

-- (4): the transferee must transmit the notice and pay; the transferor company must register. "After" is the earliest day, not a last day (see `s 215(4) the first day on which the transferee must act`); the last day of the first two is the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found`, counted from the day the trace starts, which a caller takes to be that earliest day; the registering is "thereupon", the section's own standard of time, and takes the input `the period the standard of time allows, as found` (notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
-- src:20741 | (4) Where a notice has been given by the transferee under
-- src:20742 | subsection (1) and the Court has not, on an application made by
-- src:20743 | the dissenting shareholder, ordered to the contrary, the transferee
-- src:20744 | must, after the expiration of one month after the date on which the
-- src:20745 | notice has been given or, after 14 days after a statement has been
-- src:20746 | supplied to a dissenting shareholder pursuant to subsection (2) or if an
-- src:20747 | application to the Court by the dissenting shareholder is then pending,
-- src:20748 | after that application has been disposed of —
-- src:20750 | (a) transmit a copy of the notice to the transferor company
-- src:20751 | together with an instrument of transfer executed, on behalf
-- src:20752 | of the shareholder by any person appointed by the
-- src:20753 | transferee, and on its own behalf by the transferee; and
-- src:20755 | (b) pay, allot or transfer to the transferor company the amount
-- src:20756 | or other consideration representing the price payable by the
-- src:20757 | transferee for the shares which by virtue of this section the
-- src:20758 | transferee is entitled to acquire,
@ref s 215(4) rule (src:20741-20758)
GIVEN who IS A Party
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 act`
`s 215(4) the transferee must transmit the notice and pay, allot or transfer the consideration` MEANS
    (PARTY who
     MUST `s 215(4)(a) transmit a copy of the notice to the transferor company with an instrument of transfer`
     WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY who BECAUSE "a copy of the notice was not transmitted to the transferor company with an instrument of transfer")
    RAND
    (PARTY who
     MUST `s 215(4)(b) pay, allot or transfer to the transferor company the amount or other consideration`
     WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY who BECAUSE "the amount or other consideration was not paid, allotted or transferred to the transferor company")

-- src:20760 | and the transferor company must thereupon register the transferee as
-- src:20761 | the holder of those shares.
@ref s 215(4) rule company (src:20760-20761)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("thereupon") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 act`
`s 215(4) the transferor company must register the transferee as the holder of the shares` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 215(4) register the transferee as the holder of the shares`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section says "thereupon", its own standard of time, found as an input; Interpretation Act 1965 s 52 does not apply, because the section prescribes its own standard (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the transferee was not registered as the holder of the shares"

-- (5): the transferor company must pay the sums into a separate bank account (a thing done once: the time allowed is the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found` (notes/lest-without-deadline.md), so a late act reaches BREACH) and hold them in trust (a holding that continues: no deadline fits it, so it stays untimed and is marked MAINTENANCE).
-- src:20765 | (5) Any sums received by the transferor company under this section
-- src:20766 | must be paid into a separate bank account, and any such sums and any
-- src:20767 | other consideration so received must be held by the transferor
-- src:20768 | company in trust for the several persons entitled to the shares in
-- src:20769 | respect of which they were respectively received.
@ref s 215(5) rule (src:20765-20769)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 act`
`s 215(5) the transferor company must pay the sums received into a separate bank account` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 215(5) pay the sums received into a separate bank account`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the sums received were not paid into a separate bank account"

@ref s 215(5) trust rule (src:20766-20769)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 act`
`s 215(5) the transferor company must hold the sums and other consideration in trust` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 215(5) hold the sums and other consideration in trust for the persons entitled`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 215(5) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the sums and other consideration were not held in trust for the persons entitled to the shares" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: maintenance; see notes]

-- (6): the company holding the money or other consideration must transfer before the expiration of 10 years: a deadline.
-- src:20773 | (6) Where any money or other consideration is held in trust by a
-- src:20774 | company for any person under this section, the company holding the
-- src:20775 | money or other consideration may, after the expiration of 2 years and
-- src:20776 | must before the expiration of 10 years from the date on which the
-- src:20781 | money or other consideration was received by the person, transfer the
-- src:20782 | money or other consideration to the Official Receiver.
@ref s 215(6) rule (src:20773-20782)
GIVEN who IS A Party
      `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day before the 10 years expire` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 act`
`s 215(6) the company holding the money or other consideration must transfer it to the Official Receiver before the 10 years expire` MEANS
    PARTY who
    MUST `s 215(6) transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day before the 10 years expire`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY who BECAUSE "the money or other consideration was not transferred to the Official Receiver before the expiration of 10 years from the date it was received"

-- (7): the Official Receiver's duties. No time stated: the time allowed is the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found` (notes/lest-without-deadline.md), so a late act reaches BREACH.
-- src:20786 | (7) The Official Receiver must —
-- src:20788 | (a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (6) as if
-- src:20789 | the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under
-- src:20790 | section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:20791 | Dissolution Act 2018; and
-- src:20793 | (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under
-- src:20794 | subsection (6) in such manner as the Official Receiver
-- src:20795 | thinks fit and must deal with the proceeds of such sale or
-- src:20796 | disposal as if it were moneys paid to the Official Receiver
-- src:20797 | under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:20798 | Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 215(7) rule (src:20786-20798)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 210(10B) party` `s 215(7) act`
`s 215(7)(a) the Official Receiver must deal with the moneys as if they were paid under section 197` MEANS
    PARTY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver`
    MUST `s 215(7)(a) deal with the moneys received under subsection (6) as if they were paid under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver` BECAUSE "the moneys received under subsection (6) were not dealt with as if paid under section 197"

@ref s 215(7)(b) rule (src:20793-20798)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 210(10B) party` `s 215(7) act`
`s 215(7)(b) the Official Receiver must sell or dispose of the other consideration` MEANS
    PARTY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver`
    MUST `s 215(7)(b) sell or dispose of the other consideration and deal with the proceeds as if they were moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver` BECAUSE "the other consideration received under subsection (6) was not sold or disposed of, or its proceeds were not dealt with as moneys paid under section 197"

